// Package memory holds the providers that need no host: a Scheduler whose
// sleeps end at once, for the pool's tests.

// Instant is a Scheduler whose every sleep ends at once. Under it the
// pool runs as fast as its tasks can, and its tests see only what the
// jobs and the queues decide. It keeps no time: no virtual clock in std
// moves when every task sleeps (gaps G-ex-b-5), so the virtual-clock laws
// are sched's.
type Instant {}

// Sleep ends at once.
func Sleep(_ Instant, d duration) {}
